-- #1111 A-2.5 (#1092) FLAGSHIP CELL — the S0 this unit drains.
--
-- `mth` is selected from `msb` ONLY, so this occurrence unambiguously means
-- `MB.mth`.  `Blob` implements `MA` and has NO `MB` impl, so the program is
-- ill-typed and `check` must report exactly one error here:
--
--   No impl of MB for Blob; write an 'impl MB Blob'.
--
-- Hand-derived from the language rule, not read off the tool: a method
-- occurrence's interface is fixed by what the identifier resolved to, and
-- `import msa.{MA}` deliberately does not select `msa`'s `mth`.
--
-- 🚨 BEFORE THE FIX THIS FILE CHECKED CLEAN, EXIT 0 — and `run`/`build`/the built
-- binary all printed `1`, `MA`'s impl body, for a call spelled `MB.mth` on a type
-- with no `MB` impl.  The cross-module method table was keyed by the bare method
-- name and last-write-wins, so `msa` (loaded last here, because `msb`'s import
-- line comes first) owned the single `mth` row and the obligation was recorded
-- against `MA`, which `Blob` does implement.  That is the "wrong answer, no
-- error" cell of #1092's 24-cell matrix.
--
-- The two dependency modules must stay diagnostic-FREE: a bad entry must not
-- sink the batch (this gate's own property), and neither of them is at fault.
import msb.{MB, mth}
import msa.{MA}

public export data Blob = Blob

export impl MA Blob where
  mth b = 1

main = println (mth Blob)
